EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: Twisted 26.10.0 adds a rapid-reset rate limiter — assumption A1 is refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: python:3.12-slim (custom Twisted HTTP/2 server, twisted==26.10.0)
TARGET_PORT: 8443/tcp
CLIENT_TOOL: h2

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent HEADERS(END_STREAM)+RST_STREAM cycles at maximum rate on a single connection
  against a Twisted 26.10.0 HTTP/2 server. The server throttled the connection after
  the per-connection reset budget was exhausted. CPU stayed below 8% throughout.
  Memory delta < 2 MB. Probe requests on other connections responded normally. The
  global reset budget (across all connections) also blocked the many-connection pivot.
  Fix: commit 4989394, PR #12749, Twisted 26.10.0 (October 2026). Advisory:
  GHSA-vpp8-g58w-m8mp.
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("no reset rate limit") is refuted. Twisted 26.10.0
                introduces a reset-rate limiter in H2Connection.dataReceived that
                applies both per-connection and globally, closing the many-connection
                pivot.
